INT. PIGEON LOFT, ROOFTOP - DAWN

Cooing. Feathers. Three men in a cage of chicken wire.

STASYS BIRKAVS (50s, flat cap, careful) feeds grain from a tin. DONNIE FUSCO (30s, tracksuit) and FAT LEO ARMBRUSTER (40s, enormous, quiet) sit on upturned buckets.

STASYS
Nobody here is angry. Understand?

DONNIE
Nobody's angry.

STASYS
The money is a number on paper. I like birds more than numbers.

LEO
(muttering)
Birds don't lend.

STASYS
No. They return. That is the difference.

DONNIE
(to the room)
So we're square? Everyone square?

STASYS
(smiling)
Of course. Leo, the bucket.

Leo lifts his bucket. Underneath, a revolver, and beneath that, an envelope fat with cash. Donnie's smile slides off his face.
